From c65a1f168a9bf3af09b4c710d4fc9f5d0bc74100 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:18:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): stamp portable writer_run_uid on worker comments
 so replicas keep active_pr [daveey]

commented.payload.writer_run_id is a source-database task_runs.id; sync remaps
task_events.run_id but not the payload, so on a replica the integer could name
another card's run and the owner's PR comment was classed as a foreign FYI,
dropping the active_pr respawn hold (fail open).

add_comment now also stamps writer_run_uid (task_runs.uid) when the board has
one. _foreign_pr_comment_ids and own_comment_ids (live comment bridge) decide
by that uid when present, with no fallback to the integer when it is
present-but-unusable/mismatched; uid-less legacy comments keep the integer
behaviour.

Tests: new test_kanban_pr_comment_writer_uid_sync (offset-id sync regression,
foreign real uid, invalid uid no-fallback, legacy, unattributed FYI, live
bridge). PR545/PR607 sync transports no longer re-add the PR comment at the
destination.
